WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.192
Larger dense models can improve difficult reasoning, multilingual work, coding, and robustness,

00:00:07.192 --> 00:00:11.177
but they require much more memory and serving infrastructure.

00:00:11.177 --> 00:00:19.522
The important question is whether the quality improvement justifies the added latency, cost, and operational complexity.

00:00:19.522 --> 00:00:28.462
The operational cost grows too: larger models can mean more G P U's, slower startup, more complex serving,

00:00:28.462 --> 00:00:30.452
and higher latency under load.
